_collections/
_index/
_plan/

# --- omniweave state that must never reach a pull request -----------------
# 11-repo-layout.md section 1.1: ".omniweave/ · *.owstore* · $OMNIWEAVE_HOME never inside
# the repo". A tracked store is a corpus committed to git; it fails `ow doctor` with
# OW-S-060 at runtime (00-vision V01-16) and this file is what stops it reaching a PR at all.
.omniweave/
*.owstore*

# $OMNIWEAVE_HOME defaults to ~/.omniweave (charter.md, "Names fixed here"); an operator who
# repoints it at the checkout still gets no tracked bytes.
.omniweave-home/

# --- generated package data ------------------------------------------------
# The first-party release manifest is generated into src/ by tools/gen_first_party.py during
# the `build` job (11-repo-layout.md section 7.2), so a workspace checkout has none and every
# first-party driver there is `unpinned`.
packages/omniweave-core/src/omniweave_core/drivers/first_party.toml

# --- Python / uv -----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
wheelhouse/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ruff_cache/

# --- generated fixture corpora ---------------------------------------------
# 13-quality.md:586-589: every generator under fixtures/gen/ writes to fixtures/generated/,
# "which is .gitignored", and fixtures/gen/EXPECTED.sha256 pins each output "so a generator
# change is a one-line visible diff rather than a silent corpus change". The 5,000-page PDF is
# ~29 MB against Tier A's 64 MB total (11-repo-layout.md:383), so committing it would spend half
# the corpus budget on bytes a script reproduces in a second.
fixtures/generated/
